%% title: `CLI Bootstrap State Machine`
%% summary: Same-host caller bootstrap before any daemon request can run.
%% commentary: This machine models `CliComposition::bootstrap()` plus `DaemonSupervisor::ensure_daemon_available_with_traceability()`. Every terminal is caller-visible and QA should be able to force each edge with connect misses, launch-lock contention, spawn failure, or successful connect.
%% notes: states are caller-visible bootstrap states | every terminal maps to a typed caller result | doctor only runs after DaemonReachable
%% recovery_rules: If bootstrap ends in a failure terminal, return a typed caller error with recovery text and do not attempt doctor. | If bootstrap reaches DaemonReachable, the active command may run and doctor may return a report.
%% terminal_classes: BootstrapTimedOut is a caller-facing launch-gate timeout error. | AutoStartFailed is a caller-facing daemon auto-start error. | DaemonReachable is the only success terminal for bootstrap.
%% sets: daemon
flowchart TD
    A["<b>BootstrapPending</b><br/>caller entered CliComposition::bootstrap()"] --> B["TryConnect"]
    B -->|connect_success| S["DaemonReachable
caller: continue command
doctor: may return report"]
    B -->|connect_miss| C["LaunchGateLoop"]
    C -->|retry_connect_success| S
    C -->|launch_lock_acquired| D["LaunchGateOwned"]
    C -->|deadline_expired while launch lock contended| E["BootstrapTimedOut
caller: daemon_launch_gate_rejected
doctor: no report"]
    D -->|connect_success before spawn| S
    D -->|connect_miss before spawn| F["AutoStartPending"]
    F -->|spawn_ok and publish_connect_success| S
    F -->|spawn_error| G["AutoStartFailed
caller: daemon_auto_start_failed
doctor: no report"]
    F -->|publish_wait_timeout| G

    classDef happy fill:#14532d,color:#ffffff,stroke:#14532d,stroke-width:2px;
    classDef error fill:#7f1d1d,color:#ffffff,stroke:#7f1d1d,stroke-width:2px;
    classDef neutral fill:#e2e8f0,color:#111827,stroke:#334155,stroke-width:2px;

    class A,S happy;
    class E,G error;
    class B,C,D,F neutral;
